WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.740
Welcome to Grade 8 English, Unit
1: Languages and Communication.

2
00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:08.420
Welcome to Unit 1 of your Year
8 English course at Ehel Academy.

3
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:15.120
In this unit you will explore the powerful theme of
languages and communication - how people share ideas,

4
00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:22.040
how rumours spread, and how the truth can be lost or
found depending on how carefully we listen and speak.

5
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:30.000
You will read a compelling story set in Mogadishu, learn
important grammar structures, build a rich vocabulary,

6
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.040
and practise all four...

7
00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.920
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:39.500
By the end of this unit,

9
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:45.480
you will be able to summarise the central ideas and
important details in languages and communication texts..

10
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.160
you will also support inferences and
comparisons with relevant text evidence..

11
00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:55.100
you will also use grade 8 vocabulary
accurately in discussion and writing..

12
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.880
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:06.640
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
concise, barricade, zeal, longevity, definition, allot.

14
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:12.000
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:15.840
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:23.500
The reading sequence includes Languages and Communication:
source text 1 and Languages and Communication: source text 2.

17
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.080
Read actively.

18
00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:29.780
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:33.700
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:38.500
The first language focus is What Are Contrast Conjunctions?.

21
00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:42.720
Although, while, and whereas are called contrast conjunctions.

22
00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:48.860
They connect two clauses (parts of a sentence)
that express different or surprising ideas.

23
00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:56.340
They are essential tools for showing that two things can
be true at the same time even when they seem to conflict.

24
00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:03.860
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

25
00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:08.740
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1: Contrast Debate.

26
00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:13.680
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

27
00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:17.560
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

28
00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:21.140
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

29
00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:22.640
You are ready to begin.

30
00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:28.960
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

31
00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:31.520
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

32
00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:37.731
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
